 "title": "BAW56, BAV70, BAV99: dual 70 V small-signal switching diodes in SOT-23",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev. 2.1",
  "pages": 4
 },
 "summary": "Three pairs of silicon switching diodes in one three-lead SOT-23 package, differing only in how the two junctions are joined: BAW56 shares the anodes, BAV70 shares the cathodes, BAV99 puts the two diodes in series with the midpoint brought out. Each is rated 70 V reverse and 200 mA forward, with reverse recovery of 6 ns at most and terminal capacitance of 1.5 pF at most. They are aimed at fast, general-purpose signal switching.",
