 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Configurations",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All three types hold two identical junctions. BAW56 joins both anodes to pin 3 with the cathodes on pins 1 and 2; BAV70 joins both cathodes to pin 3 with the anodes on pins 1 and 2; BAV99 runs from the anode on pin 1 through pin 3 to the cathode on pin 2."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each type carries a two-character code on the body: A1 for BAW56, A4 for BAV70, A7 for BAV99. A solid dot on the body identifies a part moulded in green compound."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The full 225 mW is allowed up to 25 °C ambient, falling in a straight line to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Packing",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Parts ship in embossed carrier tape of carbon-filled, static-dissipative polycarbonate, sealed with a multilayer heat-activated cover tape. The standard reel is 7 inch (17.8 cm), 3,000 parts, made of anti-static coated clear polystyrene."
  }
 ],
